Author-Name: Rodomanov, Anton
Author-Email: nikita.doikov@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, ICTEAM
Author-Name: Nesterov, Yurii
Author-Email: yurii.nesterov@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, LIDAM/CORE, Belgium
Title: Subgradient ellipsoid method for nonsmooth convex problems
Abstract: In this paper, we present a new ellipsoid-type algorithm for solving nonsmooth problems with convex structure. Examples of such problems include nonsmooth con- vex minimization problems, convex-concave saddle-point problems and variational inequalities with monotone operator. Our algorithm can be seen as a combination of the standard Subgradient and Ellipsoid methods. However, in contrast to the latter one, the proposed method has a reasonable convergence rate even when the dimen- sionality of the problem is sufficiently large. For generating accuracy certificates in our algorithm, we propose an efficient technique, which ameliorates the previously known recipes (Nemirovski in Math Oper Res 35(1):52–78, 2010).
Keywords: Subgradient method ; Ellipsoid method ; Accuracy certificates ; Separating oracle ; Convex optimization ; Nonsmooth optimization ; Saddle-point problems ; Variational inequalities
Note: In: Mathematical Programming, 2023, vol. 199, p. 305-341
Length: 37
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 3236
Creation-Date: 2023-01-01
DOI: https://doi.org/10.1007/s10107-022-01833-4
