Author-Name: Nunes Grapiglia, Geovani 
Author-Email: nikita.doikov@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, ICTEAM
Author-Name: Nesterov, Yurii
Author-Email: yurii.nesterov@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, LIDAM/CORE, Belgium
Title: Tensor methods for minimizing convex functions with Hölder continuous higher-order derivatives
Abstract: In this paper we study $p$-order methods for unconstrained minimization of convex functions that are $p$-times differentiable $(p ≥ 2)$ with $\nu$-Hölder continuous $p$th derivatives. We propose tensor schemes with and without acceleration. For the schemes without acceleration, we establish iteration complexity bounds of ${\Os}(\epsilon^{-1/(p+\nu-1)})$ for reducing the functional residual below a given $\epsilon \in (0,1)$. Assuming that $\nu$ is known, we obtain an improved complexity bound of ${\Os}(\epsilon^{-1/(p+\nu)})$ for the corresponding accelerated scheme. For the case in which $\nu$ is unknown, we present a universal accelerated tensor scheme with iteration complexity of ${\Os}(\epsilon^{-p/[(p+1)(p+\nu-1)]})$. A lower complexity bound of ${\Os}(\epsilon^{-2/[3(p+\nu)-2])$ is also obtained for this problem class.
Keywords: Unconstrained minimization ; high-order methods ; tensor methods ; Hölder condition ; worst-case global complexity bounds
Note: In: SIAM Journal on Optimization, 2020, vol. 30(4), p. 2750-2779
Length: 30
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 3237
Creation-Date: 2023-01-01
DOI: https://doi.org/10.1137/19M1259432
Handle: RePEc:cor:louvrp:3237

