Title: Cooperative product games
Abstract: A cooperative product game is a transferable utility game defined by associating the product of given players’ coefficient to coalitions. This idea has been introduced by Rosales, D. ([2014] Cooperative product games, unpublished mimeo, www.academia.edu/40176429) where he investigates the core. Here, we analyze a corrected definition of a product game and cover the Shapley value to which we provide an axiomatic foundation.
Keywords: Product games ; core ; Shapley value
